{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:0.2", "PA_ja_29:0.3"], "en": "The First Book (Ekakanipāta), The Chapter on the Antelope (Kuruṅgavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:0.4"], "en": "9. The Kaṇha Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:1.1", "PA_ja_29:1.2"], "en": "“Whichever way the heavy burden is borne, whichever way the deep path winds, [therein lies the way].”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:1.3"], "en": "\"Then indeed they yoke the black ox,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:1.4"], "en": "and he indeed bears that burden.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_29:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the Kaṇha Jātaka, the ninth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
